I don't have one of these, so correct me if I'm wrong...  couldn't you
take a USB flash drive, create 2 or 3 partitions, an ext2/3 for linux,
an NTFS or FAT16/32 for windows, and/or HFS/HFS+ for Mac (omit any as
necessary), install a copy of nethack on each partition, then plug
into any USB compatible computer.  This is like a multi-system version
of your solution...  the only downside is lack of bones/savefile
portability between OSs, which has nothing to do with the use of a USB
flash drive in the first place.

Checking my installations (linux and mac, windows will differ), I use
about 1400 bytes for the nethack executable script, and about 6.2 MB
for /usr/games/lib/nethackdir, and that has several bones and save
files.  Looking at my iBook, I only see about 2.7 MB in nethackdir
(this copy only rarely used).  A 128 MB USB flash drive won't cost
more than $30-40, depending on where you buy it... and you can use it
for other necessities, such as your ssh keys!

